smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-rain-eat-through-protective-coatings-on-metal-structures-researchers-propose-a-new-idea-electrically-charged-droplets-180989434/</link><description>长期以来，科学家们将雨水造成的损害归因于酸性物质的物理磨损和化学降解。一项新研究提供了第三种想法，可以帮助研究人员开发更耐用的涂层并保存重要物品</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-rain-eat-through-protective-coatings-on-metal-structures-researchers-propose-a-new-idea-electrically-charged-droplets-180989434/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员已经找到了如何利用地球磁场来识别古代陶器的赝品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-determine-how-to-spot-fake-ancient-pottery-using-the-earths-magnetic-field-180989441/</link><description>几千年来，磁北极发生了变化，在构成粘土古物的矿物中留下了线索</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 11:45:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-determine-how-to-spot-fake-ancient-pottery-using-the-earths-magnetic-field-180989441/</guid></item><item><title>您的部分性格已编码在您的基因中。大量分析将特征与 1,200 多种常见遗传变异联系起来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/part-of-your-ersonality-is-encoded-in-your-genes-huge-analysis-links-characteristics-to-more-than-1200-common-genetic-variants-180989450/</link><description>一项新的荟萃分析汇集了超过一百万人的数据，以研究 DNA 与“五大”人格特征之间的交叉：对经验的开放性、责任心、外向性、宜人性和神经质</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 11:37:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/part-of-your-ersonality-is-encoded-in-your-genes-huge-analysis-links-characteristics-to-more-than-1200-common-genetic-variants-180989450/</guid></item><item><title>科学家重现了侏罗纪昆虫失传已久的鸣叫声。聆听 1.65 亿年前的模拟音景</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-recreated-the-long-lost-chirps-of-jurassic-insects-listen-to-the-simulated-soundscape-of-165-million-years-ago-180989445/</link><description>通过人工智能和对化石翅膀的仔细建模，研究人员重现了一些已灭绝的类似螽斯的昆虫可能如何发出噪音</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 20:08:40 GMT</pubDa