/pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-discover-a-4000-year-old-tomb-with-a-false-door-at-egypts-ancient-saqqara-necropolis-180989438/</guid></item><item><title>第二次世界大战的糖配给数据表明，在生命早期限制甜食的摄入量可以降低患痴呆症和癌症的风险</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/world-war-ii-sugar-rationing-data-hints-that-limiting-intake-of-the-sweet-stuff-early-in-life-lowers-the-risk-of-dementia-and-cancer-180989431/</link><description>在 1953 年 9 月之前的大约十年里，英国限制了食糖的购买。科学家研究了配给期间和配给后出生的人的健康结果</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:48:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/world-war-ii-sugar-rationing-data-hints-that-limiting-intake-of-the-sweet-stuff-early-in-life-lowers-the-risk-of-dementia-and-cancer-180989431/</guid></item><item><title>珊瑚显示近几十年来厄尔尼诺现象变得更加严重，可能是因为人类使地球变暖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/corals-reveal-el-nino-events-have-become-stronger-in-recent-decades-probably-because-humans-have-been-heating-up-the-planet-180989432/</link><description>研究人员利用加拉帕戈斯珊瑚中捕获的元素来了解过去千年气候的自然波动。他们暗示，与工业化前时期相比，过去 40 年的变异性有所增加</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/corals-reveal-el-nino-events-have-become-stronger-in-recent-decades-probably-because-humans-have-been-heating-up-the-planet-180989432/</guid></item><item><title>对狗过敏？这些经过基因编辑的比格犬可以为您梦想中的不会引发鼻涕的犬类伴侣铺平道路</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/allergic-to-dogs-these-gene-edited-beagles-could-pave-the-way-to-your-dream-canine-companion-that-wont-trigger-sniffles-180989303/</link><description>遗传学家改变了阿尔菲和贝利的 DNA，使他们不会产生主要的过敏原。然而，像它们这样的犬科动物目前还没有商业化，一些专家对改变动物基因表示道德担忧</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 19:12:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/allergic-to-dogs-these-gene-edited-beagles-could-pave-the-way-to-your-dream-canine-companion-that-wont-trigger-sniffles-180989303/</guid></item><item><title>这位 91 岁的老人在阿巴拉契亚小道徒步旅行时摔倒了 71 次。他刚刚成为完成 2,190 英里长途跋涉的最年长的人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-91-year-old-man-fell-71-times-while-hiking-appalachian-trail-he-just-became-oldest-person-complete-2190-mile-trek-180989428/</link><description>戴尔·桑德斯 (Dale Sanders) 在不到一年的时间里完成了这次加息。绰号“灰胡子”的他对抗衰老的耐力并不陌生</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:24:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-91-year-old-man-fell-71-times-while-hiking-appalachian-trail-he-just-became-oldest-person-complete-2190-mile-trek-180989428/</guid></item><item><title>倡导者称，洛杉矶的弗兰克·劳埃德·赖特住宅面临“因疏忽而被拆除”的危险</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-frank-lloyd-wright-house-in-la-is-in-danger-of-demolition-by-neglect-say-advocates-180989429/</link><description>这位有远见的人以他负担得起的乌索尼亚风格设计了这套两居室、一间浴室。这是洛杉矶唯一的此类房屋</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 17:18:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-frank-lloyd-wright-house-in-la-is-in-danger-of-demolition-by-neglect-say-advocates-180989429/</guid></item><item><title>火星南半部的地下异常温暖。 “热异常”可能解释了为什么地球的半球看起来如此不同</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mars-southern-half-is-weirdly-warm-underground-the-thermal-anomaly-might-explain-why-the-planets-hemispheres-look-so-different-180989424/</link><description>研究人员使用了一种新颖的技术来弄清楚这颗红色星球内部正在发生什么。这项工作表明，南半球内部比北半球内部温度高数百度，并且部分熔化</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:47:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mars-southern-half-is-weirdly-warm-underground-the-thermal-anomaly-might-explain-why-the-planets-hemispheres-look-so-different-180989424/</guid></item></channel></rss>